    "specPath": "specs/036-mid-plan-acquisition/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 002, 003 and 004 (R-16), for #76 child B1 under owner decision R-40 (OD-3 of #76). A plan may declare bounded acquisition steps that ask a host-implemented acquisition source for more context between steps, with requests built only from exact values and literals, and a tiered widening construct that tries a finite, declared list of increasingly broad requests (optionally across sources) until a stop condition holds, never relaxing protected constraints. Paging is bounded by pages, items and a stop condition. Adds acquisition operations to spec 032's source descriptor (`rustev.source/1`), acquisition request and page documents, the `compose_key@1` operator, a typed `skipped` outcome, compile-time call, item, byte, deadline and cost budgets, and the in-process `AcquisitionSource` seam a later remote protocol (#76 A2) carries. Every page is recorded and captured by request identity; offline replay never dispatches and an uncaptured request is `missing_evidence`. Adds to the #76 track versions introduced by spec 032 (source 1, definition 2, plan 3, evidence 2, run 3, exact 2), introduces the track version `rustev.replay/2`, and admits every plan 3 decision to capture and replay, lifting spec 032's interim `capture_unsupported` refusal. Plans that use no #76 construct keep byte-identical documents and `PlanId`s. Approved (A-33); implementation is in progress.\n",
    "title": "Mid-plan context acquisition and tiered widening (amends 002, 003 and 004)"
  },
